      "text": "To determine the day of the week for December 23 if Thanksgiving is on Thursday, November 23, we need to calculate the number of days between November 23 and December 23 and then find the day of the week that corresponds to that number of days, given that November 23 is a Thursday.\n\nFirst, we calculate the number of days from November 23 to December 23:\n- November has 30 days, so the number of days from November 1 to November 23 is 23 - 1 + 1 = 23 days.\n- The number of days from November 23 to December 23 is 30 days - 23 days = 7 days.\n- Adding these together, we get 23 + 7 = 30 days.\n\nNext, we need to determine the day of the week 30 days after Thursday. Since a week has 7 days, we can find the remainder when 30 is divided by 7:\n\\[ 30 \\div 7 = 4 \\text{ R } 2 \\]\nThis means that 30 days is equivalent to 4 weeks and 2 extra days. Starting from Thursday, moving forward 4 weeks takes us back to Thursday, and then 2 more days from Thursday brings us to Friday.\n\nTherefore, December 23 is on a \\boxed{Friday}.",
