      "text": "To determine the day of the week for December 23 given that Thanksgiving is on Thursday, November 23, we need to calculate the number of days between these two dates and then find the corresponding day of the week.\n\n1. **Calculate the number of days between November 23 and December 23:**\n\n   - November has 30 days. From November 23 to November 30 is \\(30 - 23 + 1 = 8\\) days.\n   - December has 31 days. From December 1 to December 23 is \\(23\\) days.\n   - Therefore, the total number of days between November 23 and December 23 is \\(8 + 23 = 31\\) days.\n\n2. **Determine the day of the week after 31 days:**\n\n   - Since there are 7 days in a week, we can find the remainder when 31 is divided by 7.\n   - \\(31 \\div 7 = 4\\) with a remainder of \\(3\\).\n   - A remainder of 3 means that 31 days from a given day is equivalent to the same day of the week but 3 days later.\n   - November 23 is a Thursday. Three days later, we add 3 days to Thursday:\n     - Thursday + 1 day = Friday\n     - Friday + 1 day = Saturday\n     - Saturday + 1 day = Sunday\n\nTherefore, December 23 falls on a \\(\\boxed{\\text{Sunday}}\\).",
