      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "### Problem:\nTo determine the day of the week for December 23 given that Thanksgiving is on Thursday, November 23, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the number of days between Thanksgiving and December 23:**\n\n   - Thanksgiving falls on Monday, November 23.\n   - December 23 falls some number of days after November 23.\n\n2. **Find the total number of days between the two dates:**\n\n   - Calculate the number of days from November 23 to December 23.\n   - From November 23 to December 1, it's a 25-day period (November has 30 days, so from November 23 to December 1 is \\(30 - 23 + 1 = 8\\) days, but we need to count the remaining 23 days from November 23 to December 23).\n\n   Therefore, the total number of days between November 23 and December 23 is:\n   \\[\n   25 \\text{ days}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine the day of the week using the modulus operation:**\n\n   - The day of the week advances by 1 day for each day of the month.\n   - Starting from a Monday (November 23), we count forward by 1 day each day.\n\n   The formula to find the day of the week after 25 days on a Monday effectively is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Day of the week} = (\\text{Initial day of the week} + \\text{Number of days} \\mod 7)\n   \\]\n   Here, the initial day is Monday (0 for Monday, 1 for Tuesday, etc.):\n   \\[\n   \\text{Day of the week after 25 days} = (1 + 25 \\mod 7) \\mod 7\n   \\]\n   Calculate \\(25 \\mod 7\\):\n   \\[\n   25 \\div 7 = 3 \\text{ remainder } 4 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 25 \\mod 7 = 4\n   \\]\n   Thus:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Day of the week after 25 days} = (1 + 4) \\mod 7 = 5 \\mod 7 = 5\n   \\]\n   This is equivalent to the day of the week that is 5 days after Monday. Counting forward, we find:\n   \\[\n   5 \\text{ days after Monday is Saturday}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, December 23 falls on a \\(\\boxed{\\text{Saturday}}\\).",
